3. Approach 2 — Better Brute Force O(n²)

We don't need the third loop.

While extending the subarray, we can maintain the current minimum and maximum.

For each starting index i:

min = nums[i]
max = nums[i]

Then move j forward:

min = Math.min(min, nums[j])
max = Math.max(max, nums[j])

Now we immediately know the range.

